and management</article-title><source>Neurosurgery</source><year>1987</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>747</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3601022</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Menezes</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Graf</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacoby</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></name><name><surname>Cornell</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Management of veinof Galen aneurysms: Report of two cases</article-title><source>J Neurosurg</source><year>1981</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>457</fpage><lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7264737</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Portnoy</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Herion</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Neurological manifestations in sickle-cell disease - with a review of the literature and emphasis on the prevalence of hemiplegia</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1972</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>643</fpage><lpage>52</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4640322</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balkaran</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Char</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Morris</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>PW</given-names></name><name><surname>Serjeant</surname><given-names>BE</given-names></name><name><surname>Serjeant</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><article-t